{
  "typeCheckingMode": "strict",
  "pythonVersion": "3.13",
  "include": ["learning/code", "learning/capstone/code"],
  // Why these four categories are off, measured against learning/code/requirements.txt's
  // exact pins (redis==8.0.1, pymongo==4.17.0, cassandra-driver==3.30.1, boto3==1.43.56,
  // psycopg[binary]==3.3.4, duckdb==1.5.5, pyarrow==25.0.0):
  //
  // Re-enabling all four with nothing else changed originally produced 384 strict-mode
  // errors across 53 of this topic's 86 Python files (verified 2026-07-27, pyright 1.1.411).
  // Of those 53, 7 imported no NoSQL driver at all and were flagged purely because their own
  // dataclass fields left an empty-container `default_factory` unparameterized (e.g.
  // `field(default_factory=list)` on a `list[str]`-annotated field) -- nothing about that
  // was actually a stub-quality problem, so those 7 files (ex-20, ex-23, ex-43, ex-55, ex-57,
  // ex-73, ex-74) were fixed DIRECTLY, not suppressed: each `default_factory` now carries its
  // own type parameter (`default_factory=list[str]`, `default_factory=dict[str, int]`, etc.),
  // which pyright resolves without help from this file. Re-verified 2026-07-27: re-enabling
  // all four categories now produces 377 errors across 46 of 86 files -- the 7 driver-free
  // files no longer appear at all.
  //
  // The remaining 46 files are NOT explained by "cassandra-driver/boto3/pyarrow ship zero
  // type stubs" alone -- those three account for only 17 of the 46 affected files (plus 7
  // more mixed with a typed library). The other 22 files import ONLY redis and/or pymongo
  // (both DO ship py.typed) but still error, because their own upstream stubs leave several
  // return/parameter types partially unknown -- e.g. redis.Redis.pipeline() resolves
  // shard_hint as `Unknown | None`, and pymongo.MongoClient resolves as the unparameterized
  // `MongoClient[Unknown]`. This is imprecision in the upstream stub, not a missing stub.
  // Because a majority of this topic's files are affected for reasons that have nothing to
  // do with cassandra-driver/boto3/pyarrow specifically, scoping the suppression only to
  // those three libraries' call sites (the ex-88/ex-89 narrow-disclosed-# pyright: ignore
  // pattern) would still leave most of the 377 errors unaddressed; scoping via
  // `executionEnvironments` would need to include roughly 46 of 86 files, which is no
  // narrower than this topic-wide suppression in practice. This suppression stays global
  // to `learning/code` and `learning/capstone/code`, touches only the four `reportUnknown*`
  // / `reportMissingTypeStubs` categories, and leaves every other strict-mode category
  // (including reportUnknownParameterType, used by the ex-88/ex-89 narrow ignores) fully
  // enforced.
  "reportMissingTypeStubs": false,
  "reportUnknownMemberType": false,
  "reportUnknownVariableType": false,
  "reportUnknownArgumentType": false
}
